(6424121, 952041, 20608, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Techo:</b></div><hr/><i> Nicely done. The composition and point of focus are just spot on. I like the soft look of the shot. Too much contrast ain''t always that romantic. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Couldn''t agree more. The problem with having a full gamut screen is that not everyone else can see what you see. There is no editing to this so I am extremely happy with getting it right IN CAMERA. Too many years I have relied on software to get the result I wanted.</td>', 'Originally posted by Techo: Nicely done. The composition and point of focus are just spot on. I like the soft look of the shot. Too much contrast ain''t always that romantic.   Couldn''t agree more. The problem with having a full gamut screen is that not everyone else can see what you see. There is no editing to this so I am extremely happy with getting it right IN CAMERA. Too many years I have relied on software to get the result I wanted.', '2011-05-25 04:28:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(6424127, 952114, 129171, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments. I agree with the vote and wasn\''t happy with my entry - I seem to struggle with taking photos to a theme with little notice but I\''m working on it! As for the clarity and focus - the photo was taken with reverse-lens macro so the depth of field is about 1mm! With some subjects it works or you can get away with it (I''m not allowed to post a link to examples but my blog on blogger is amoodaday and click the ''reverse lens'' field), with others it doesn''t. <br/><br/><hr/>365 project: //www.originaltake.com</td>', 'Thanks for the comments. I agree with the vote and wasn\''t happy with my entry - I seem to struggle with taking photos to a theme with little notice but I\''m working on it! As for the clarity and focus - the photo was taken with reverse-lens macro so the depth of field is about 1mm! With some subjects it works or you can get away with it (I''m not allowed to post a link to examples but my blog on blogger is amoodaday and click the ''reverse lens'' field), with others it doesn''t. 365 project: //www.originaltake.com', '2011-05-25 05:34:10.000000', NULL, 0),
